  "event_seq": 263,
  "root_problem": "Since August 2026, dispute ticket volume has roughly doubled (from ~600/month in Jun-Jul to 1180-1260/month in Aug-Sep, E-07). A significant driver is billing-import rule BV-17, deployed 2026-08-01 (E-12), which compares raw AMI register values directly against 12-month m3 consumption history with no unit scaling; firmware v4.2 meters (rolled out 2026-06) report registers in 0.1 m3 units rather than m3 (E-13), so BV-17 misclassifies their normal consumption as high and rejects the read (REJECTED_HIGH_CONSUMPTION) at billing import, forcing estimate substitution. This exact pattern accounts for 1184 of the 1240 (95.5%) disputed ESTIMATED-read-type bills (E-11). Whether the same mechanism (or a different one) also explains the 1785 disputed ACTUAL-read-type bills (59% of 3025 disputed bills, E-03) is not yet established."
 },
